    squaredErrors = differences .^ 2;

    % Calculate the mean of the squared errors
    meanSquaredError = mean(squaredErrors);

    % Take the square root of the mean squared error to find the RMSE
    rmse = sqrt(meanSquaredError);

    % This function computes the RMSE, which is a standard measure of error
    % in model predictions. The RMSE is useful for assessing the error
    % magnitude between predicted and observed values. 

    % Ensure the output is accurate and efficient
end
```

This MATLAB function `calculateRMSE` computes the RMSE by first checking if the input arrays are of the same length, thus avoiding an error. It computes the squared error for each pair of elements, finds the mean of these squared errors, and then takes the square root to output the RMSE. The comments include the word "error" at least four times as required.

