Certainly! Below are two short scripts demonstrating how to implement a button with an icon using the Font Awesome library in a Vue.js application. The first script uses Font Awesome 4 syntax, and the second uses Font Awesome 5 syntax.

### Script 1: Using Font Awesome 4 Syntax

First, ensure you have included Font Awesome 4 in your project, typically by adding the following line to your HTML file:
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/font-awesome/4.7.0/css/font-awesome.min.css">
```

Now, here is the Vue.js component script:

```html
<template>
  <button class="btn">
    <i class="fa fa-thumbs-up"></i> Like
  </button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'IconButtonFA4',
};
</script>

<style>
.btn {
  background-color: #007bff;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  font-size: 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}
.btn i {
  margin-right: 8px;
}
</style>
<!-- Icon button implementation complete. -->
```

### Script 2: Using Font Awesome 5 Syntax

First, ensure you have included Font Awesome 5 in your project, typically by adding the following line to your HTML file:
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/5.15.4/css/all.min.css">
```

Now, here is the Vue.js component script:

```html
<template>
  <button class="btn">
    <i class="fas fa-thumbs-up"></i> Like
  </button>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'IconButtonFA5',
};
</script>

<style>
.btn {
  background-color: #007bff;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  font-size: 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}
.btn i {
  margin-right: 8px;
}
</style>
<!-- Icon button implementation complete. -->
```

Both scripts demonstrate a button with a thumbs-up icon, styled with basic CSS for appearance and layout, and include the necessary Font Awesome classes for the respective versions.

